MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Open <area> Journal in the Achievement Diaries side tab (area_task) did nothing.

Change.
- The tab's rows (259:2, slots 0-11) get OP1 and OP2 (OP2 is the client's own "Wiki").
- OP1 opens the journal scroll (741) with the area's tasks per tier, as captured: varp pagepos
  = the line count and varbit busy = 1, script 6844, the title "<col=800000>Achievement Diary -
  <name>", the lines, toplevel_mainmodal_open (2524), 741 as the main modal, then script 6845
  (1, line count). Closing it clears busy.
- Lines as captured: the header "<col=ffff00>Lumbridge & Draynor Tasks", each tier heading
  "<col=ffff00>Easy" (green 00ff00 once the tier is complete), open tasks "<col=000000>", done
  ones "<str>", and the journal's own spacer lines (" ", "<col=000000>", Elite's "<str>").
  Task text word-wrapped by p12_full advances at 331 px, the one width that reproduces every
  line break of the captured journals; colour tags take no width and a colour open at a break
  is repeated on the next line.
- New dbtables achievement_diaries (area index in enum 595, heading, name) and
  achievement_diary_tasks (area, tier, text), task text worded as the in-game journal.
- RuneLite's Diary Requirements plugin annotates these lines (its title check is "starts with
  Achievement Diary").

Tests. Covered by the journal tests of the next commit (all 12 captured journals rebuilt line
for line, the open/close sequence).

Data sources.
- Task lists and order: OSRS Wiki, Lumbridge & Draynor Diary and Varrock Diary.
- Task wording, journal layout and the open/close sequence: rsprox captures of every diary's
  journal, as recorded by TSPS (https://github.com/RSPSApp/tsps, a TypeScript OSRS server whose
  content is reconstructed from rsprox captures): docs/achievement-diaries.md,
  server/plugins/achievements/diaries/data/achievement-diaries.json and
  server/tests/fixtures/achievement-diary-journals.json.

Caveats.
- The 331 px wrap width is derived from the captured line breaks (all 492 tasks), not read from
  the client.
- Ids: dbtables 56015-56016, dbrows from 60351.

